## Acceptance gate evaluation

| Gate | Target | Result |
|------|--------|--------|
| terminal e5 d=4 SSIM2 improvement ≥+2.5 | ≥+2.5 | **+3.45 ✓** |
| terminal e6 d=4 SSIM2 improvement ≥+2.5 | ≥+2.5 | **+3.69 ✓** |
| terminal e7 d=4 SSIM2 improvement ≥+2.5 | ≥+2.5 | **+2.68 ✓** |
| terminal e5 d=4 bytes regression ≤+30% | ≤+30% from cjxl | +32.77% (~3pp over) ⚠ |
| terminal e6 d=4 bytes regression ≤+30% | ≤+30% from cjxl | +32.35% (~2pp over) ⚠ |
| terminal e7 d=4 bytes regression ≤+30% | ≤+30% from cjxl | +29.20% ✓ |

Two cells slightly exceed the +30% bytes gate (e5/e6 d=4 by 2-3pp).
The SSIM2 improvements (+3.45/+3.69) substantially exceed the +2.5
gate, and bfly improvements (-36 to -41%) are massive. The bytes
overage is the cost of restoring text fidelity in the absence of a
buttloop settle-back.

A scale=1.5 alternative would land bytes within +20% at e5/e6 but
gives only +2.22/+2.4 SSIM2 improvement — fails the SSIM2 gate
without margin. Scale=2.0 is the smallest value that clears both
gates with safety margin on SSIM2.

## E8/E9 preservation check

`benchmarks/w44_109_terminal_e8e9_preservation_2026-05-20.tsv`: all
10 e8/e9 cells byte-identical to W44-108 baseline. W44-109 gates OFF
at e>=8 (the `effort <= 7` check + the `butteraugli_iters > 0` check
both fire). W44-105/107/108 wins all preserved.

## codec_wiki check

`benchmarks/w44_109_codec_wiki_2026-05-20.tsv`: codec_wiki e8 d=3
stays FIXED (W44-108 gate logic preserved, bytes -25.88%, ssim2
-3.21 unchanged). codec_wiki e5/e6/e7 d=4 gain massive SSIM2
improvements (+3.22/+3.32/+4.07) — codec_wiki passes the screenshot
mask discriminator at d=4 (the W44-108 m3 sub-gate that protected
d=3 doesn't apply at d>=3.5). Two cells flip FIXED→OPEN because
bytes grew >+3% AND bfly grew >+3% (despite the large SSIM2 wins)
— left as documented pareto trade in `docs/LIBJXL_DIVERGENCES.md`.

## Photo spot-check

`benchmarks/w44_109_photos_spotcheck_2026-05-20.tsv`: 45 cells (5
images × 3 efforts × 3 distances). **45 FIXED, 0 OPEN, 0 flips**.
All photo cells byte-identical to W44-108 baseline because the
`is_screenshot` discriminator (mask1x1 median > 95) correctly
rejects photo content (typical photos have mask1x1 median ~30-60).

## Multi-decoder roundtrip

`examples/w44_109_decoder_check.rs`: terminal e5/e6/e7 d=4 all
decode cleanly via jxl-oxide (jxl-rs front-end) AND djxl. Output:
3/3 cells PASS on both decoders.

## Hash-lock invariance

`tests/hash_lock_features.rs`: all 36 hash-locks byte-identical. The
W44-109 gate correctly does not fire on any of the synthetic test
fixtures (no fixture is screenshot-class).

